<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Dynamic Import</title>
</head>
<body>

    <button id="btn">Greet</button>
    <h1 id="result"></h1>

    <script type="module" src="main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
//JS
export function greet(name) {
    return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
  document.getElementById("btn").addEventListener("click", async () => {
    const module = await import("./greet.js");

    const result = module.greet("Abdulloh");

    document.getElementById("result").textContent = result;
});
      //SELF
      Avval button bosilishini kutamiz:

document.getElementById("btn").addEventListener("click", async () => {

Button bosilganda:

const module = await import("./greet.js");

→ greet.js shu paytda yuklanadi.

Keyin:

const result = module.greet("Abdulloh");

→ yuklangan modul ichidagi greet() funksiyasini ishlatamiz.

Nega module.greet()?

Chunki dynamic import modulni object ko‘rinishida qaytaradi:

module
 └── greet

Shuning uchun:

module.greet()
Natija

Buttonni bossak:

Hello, Abdulloh!

Oddiy import:

import { greet } from "./greet.js";

→ dastur boshida yuklanadi.

Dynamic import:

const module = await import("./greet.js");

→ kerak bo‘lgan paytda yuklanadi.

Qisqa formula:
import() → modulni yukla
await → yuklanishini kut
module.greet() → funksiyani ishlat
